<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<gpx version="1.1" creator="book_route.py" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1">
<metadata><name>Lost Valley Off-Trail Route</name><desc>or-vielbig-2e:267-2: route read from the book's text and sketch map. One trkseg per waypoint pair, in order; segment sources are in the trk desc. Geometry from OSM (ODbL, (c) OpenStreetMap contributors) and USFS EDW (public domain) where marked; 'straight' segments are off-trail connectors, not traced.</desc></metadata>
<wpt lat="43.999772" lon="-121.663687"><ele>1935.4</ele><name>Dutchman Flat Sno-Park</name><desc>source: DB trailhead pin th:dutchman-flat-sno-park (OSM way 559496151); confidence: high; pdf_page: 269; book_elev_ft: 6400; quote: From Dutchman Flat Nordic Sno-Park, ski the trail north along the east edge of the open flat (Swampy Lakes and Flagline text, same page)</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.024312" lon="-121.657374"><ele>2022.3</ele><name>Flagline Access / Flagline Trail #41 junction (map 60: trail 6 meets the Swampy Lks - Flagline trail)</name><desc>source: OSM node 1067700935 shared by Flagline Access XC trail 40.1 (way 294603184) and Flagline Trail #41 (way 299566182); 0.5 mi west of Tumalo Pass as map 60 draws; confidence: high; pdf_page: 269; quote: From the lower end of Little Meadow ski east and uphill on the Swampy Lakes Trail through a sinuous meadow to the large meadow at its head.</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.029000" lon="-121.655000"><ele>2035.4</ele><name>Windy Gap</name><desc>source: DEM: 6,730 ft gap between the 7,005 ft butte (map's 7048') and the 6,970 ft butte to the east; map 60 labels Windy Gap just north of the trail; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 269; quote: Leave the trail and bear north into the east arm of the meadow, following almost continuous meadows, somewhere along here passing through Windy Gap</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.033500" lon="-121.653000"><ele>2051.9</ele><name>Lost Valley, east of the low forested ridge</name><desc>source: DEM valley floor 6,720-6,750 ft east of the 7,005 ft butte; map 60's LOST VALLEY dots; confidence: low; pdf_page: 269; quote: and along the east side of a low, forested ridge</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.038500" lon="-121.650500"><ele>2028.6</ele><name>Lost Valley, north end</name><desc>source: DEM valley floor about 6,650 ft; placed to keep the line in the valley; confidence: low; pdf_page: 269; quote: following almost continuous meadows</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.043500" lon="-121.660000"><ele>2061.4</ele><name>Crater Ditch Flat (west part, near road 370)</name><desc>source: DEM level ground 6,740-6,780 ft south-east of Moon Mountain (7,270 ft DEM at 44.050,-121.668); 0.4 mi east of the OSM NF 370 / 378 junction (map 60's 6780'), where the sketch's dots end; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 269; book_elev_ft: 6780; quote: You will eventually reach Crater Ditch Flat, a huge, level meadow at the southeast foot of Moon Mountain.</desc></wpt>
<trk><name>Lost Valley Off-Trail Route</name><desc>1. Dutchman Flat Sno-Park -&gt; Flagline Access / Flagline Trail #41 junction (map 60: trail 6 meets the Swampy Lks - Flagline trail): osm (high), 2.16 mi | 2. Flagline Access / Flagline Trail #41 junction (map 60: trail 6 meets the Swampy Lks - Flagline trail) -&gt; Windy Gap: straight (medium), 0.34 mi | 3. Windy Gap -&gt; Lost Valley, east of the low forested ridge: straight (low), 0.33 mi | 4. Lost Valley, east of the low forested ridge -&gt; Lost Valley, north end: straight (low), 0.37 mi | 5. Lost Valley, north end -&gt; Crater Ditch Flat (west part, near road 370): straight (medium), 0.58 mi</desc>
